  "strategy": "# 1. Approach and Rationale\nThe strategy employs a multi-stage optimization approach to improve the C\u2085 bound by combining:\n\n1. **Initial Exploration via Particle Swarm Optimization (PSO)**: PSO excels at exploring non-convex landscapes and escaping local minima through its swarm-based movement rules. We initialize a small swarm with adaptive population control to balance exploration and computational efficiency.\n\n2. **Convex Relaxation Refinement**: After PSO identifies promising regions, we apply a line search with exact gradient information to refine solutions in a convexified neighborhood around top candidates. This leverages the precision of convex optimization while maintaining global optimality guarantees.\n\n3. **Efficient Sampling Strategy**: We use a discretization resolution of n_points=150, balancing accuracy and computation time. The initial_h_values construction serves as a warm start to accelerate convergence.\n\n# 2. Mathematical Specification\n- **Decision Variable**: h \u2208 [0,1]^{n_points} with \u2211h = n_points/2\n- **Objective**: Minimize C = (2/n_points) * max_{k} (h \u2217 (1-h))[k]\n- **Constraints**:\n  - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 \u2200i\n  - \u2211h = n_points/2\n\nThe convolution operation uses numpy's correlate with mode='full', scaled by (2/n_points).\n\n# 3. Implementation Procedure\n## Initialization (n_points=150)\n1. Interpolate initial_h_values (if provided) to 150 points.\n2. Initialize PSO swarm:\n   - 20 particles with positions uniformly sampled near initial_h_values\n   - Velocities initialized to small random values\n   - Best individual and swarm positions tracked\n\n## PSO Optimization Loop (200 iterations)\n1. Clip particle positions to [0,1] and normalize to maintain \u2211h = 75\n2. Evaluate C for each particle\n3. Update best positions and apply PSO velocity updates:\n   - V_i(t+1) = w*V_i(t) + c1*r1*(P_i(t) - X_i(t)) + c2*r2*(P_g(t) - X_i(t))\n   - X_i(t+1) = X_i(t) + V_i(t+1)\n4. Decay inertia weight w from 0.9 to 0.4\n5. Periodically add adaptive noise to maintain exploration\n\n## Refinement Stage\n1. Collect top 5 particles with lowest C\n2. For each, perform line search along random directions in convexified space\n\n# 4. Search Choices and Variations\n- **Swarm Adaptation**: Reduce particle count by 50% if no improvement in 50 iterations\n- **Line Search**: Use golden-section search for continuous improvement\n- **Convexification**: Apply to h variables to enable gradient-based refinement\n\n# 5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n- **Initialization**: 10 seconds\n- **PSO Loop**: 150 iterations @ 2 sec/iter = 300 seconds\n- **Refinement**: 500 seconds\n- **Termination Checks**: After 500 sec, return best solution found\n\n# 6. Validation and Return Contract\n- Final candidate evaluated with strict C metric\n- Ensure feasibility with h \u2208 [0,1] and \u2211h=75\n- Verify C improves or matches initial construction",
